      "en": "The shape you will meet most: orders (an array), each with items (an array). To make «one line per product» (like n8n’s Split Out): loop over the orders and, inside each, over its items, building a new object with the order’s data plus the product’s. You will write this in a Code node when a ready-made node does not do what you need."
